WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.790
Find a seated or resting position that is workable, not perfect.

2
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.950
Patience here does not mean tolerating harm or delaying a needed action.

3
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:16.750
It means staying for one chosen, ordinary moment without demanding that it move faster.

4
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:26.563
Feel the body arriving on its support.

5
00:00:28.263 --> 00:00:33.563
Notice one place that already feels settled and one place that is still adjusting.

6
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:56.250
Choose a neutral sensation to accompany: the hands touching, the feet on the floor, or breath moving somewhere in the body.

7
00:01:12.047 --> 00:01:14.097
Stay until the sensation changes once.

8
00:01:15.797 --> 00:01:21.057
Perhaps pressure shifts, temperature becomes clearer, or an inhale turns toward an exhale.

9
00:01:22.757 --> 00:01:24.637
There is no need to make the change happen.

10
00:01:43.593 --> 00:01:49.423
Notice any urge to move on, check the time, improve the practice, or reach the next instruction.

11
00:01:51.123 --> 00:01:54.443
Let the urge be present for one breath before deciding anything.

12
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.670
Patience can be small.

13
00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:19.180
Try the phrase: I can stay for this one breath.

14
00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.950
Let the sentence end when the breath ends.

15
00:02:41.907 --> 00:02:43.587
Begin again with the next breath.

16
00:02:45.287 --> 00:02:46.237
Not forever.

17
00:02:47.937 --> 00:02:49.687
Not until everything is resolved.

18
00:02:51.387 --> 00:02:54.867
Only this ordinary beginning, middle, and end.

19
00:03:16.983 --> 00:03:19.603
If discomfort needs an adjustment, make it slowly.

20
00:03:21.303 --> 00:03:25.943
Patience includes responding carefully rather than refusing what the body is saying.

21
00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.630
Listen to a sound until it ends or fades from attention.

22
00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.940
Notice the space before another sound becomes clear.

23
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.950
You are not waiting for a special event.

24
00:04:15.066 --> 00:04:18.016
Perhaps thoughts are forecasting how long something in life will take.

25
00:04:19.716 --> 00:04:23.236
Acknowledge planning, then return to the immediate contact under the body.

26
00:04:42.192 --> 00:04:45.582
Feel the difference between waiting with tension and waiting with room.

27
00:04:47.282 --> 00:04:54.272
Soften one unnecessary grip in the jaw, hands, shoulders, or belly without requiring full relaxation.

28
00:05:16.388 --> 00:05:17.938
Choose three breaths.

29
00:05:19.638 --> 00:05:24.938
For each one, notice the first moment, allow the middle, and recognize the ending.

30
00:05:26.638 --> 00:05:29.628
If attention leaves, return to whichever breath is here now.

31
00:05:58.063 --> 00:05:59.103
Let counting go.

32
00:06:00.803 --> 00:06:04.133
Notice whether impatience has vanished, changed, or stayed.

33
00:06:05.833 --> 00:06:08.833
None of these outcomes determines whether you practiced well.

34
00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:32.640
Bring to mind one situation today where a pause could create a little more choice.

35
00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.170
Keep the image brief.

36
00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.730
Do not solve the whole situation here.

37
00:06:54.527 --> 00:06:59.077
Imagine feeling both feet before responding, or taking one breath before the next action.

38
00:07:00.777 --> 00:07:03.757
Patience can be a gap large enough for a wise decision.

39
00:07:25.873 --> 00:07:26.853
Return to the room.

40
00:07:28.553 --> 00:07:32.043
Notice sounds, light, and the full outline of the body.

41
00:07:33.743 --> 00:07:35.983
Let the next moment arrive without leaning toward it.

42
00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.010
Move when you choose.

43
00:07:54.710 --> 00:08:00.000
You practiced staying without becoming stuck and waiting without abandoning action.
